<Base title="Clear explanations. Checkable sources." description="How Howloop prepares educational content, handles corrections and distinguishes bank product data from financial advice."><header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / editorial policy</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">HOWLOOP · THE DETAILS</span><h1 style="max-width:900px">Clear explanations. Checkable sources.</h1></header><article class="hl-wrap hl-content"><p class="hl-page-meta">Updated 18 September 2026</p><h2>Our publishing standard</h2><p>Our aim is to explain a financial idea in plain English, give a worked example and make the assumptions visible. Articles are written for education, not to recommend a product or assess an individual’s circumstances.</p><h2>Sources</h2><p>We prefer Australian primary sources: ASIC’s Moneysmart, APRA, the Consumer Data Right register and official provider information. A guide includes links to the sources used for factual context. Examples are clearly labelled hypothetical or illustrative and are not presented as current offers.</p><h2>Data and calculations</h2><p>Public product feeds are machine-readable snapshots, not independently verified recommendations. We show retrieval dates and identify unavailable or partial data. Our <a href="/methodology">methodology</a> explains the formulas and which rate structures are supported. Calculator logic is checked against independent mathematical examples, including zero-interest cases and loan balances covered by offsets.</p><h2>Use of AI</h2><p>AI tools may assist with drafting, explanations, code and testing. AI assistance does not amount to review by a licensed financial professional. We do not claim specialist credentials or professional approval where none has been established.</p><h2>Corrections and updates</h2><p>Report a possible error through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, ideally with a source or reproducible example. When content is changed, its date should reflect the actual update. A data retrieval date records when a feed was fetched; it is not a guarantee that a bank will keep that rate.</p><h2>Commercial independence</h2><p>Provider listings are alphabetical. Published calculations are not altered to favour an advertiser. Ads, sponsored placements and affiliate links, if introduced, must be distinguishable from editorial content and disclosed in context.</p><h2>Archived material</h2><p>Older household and device guides remain accessible at their original URLs. They have a different subject area from the current money tools and should be read with their own dates and limitations in mind.</p></article></Base>
